$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
9-Ethyl-6,6-dimethyl-8-(1-methyl-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-11-oxo-6,11-dihydro-5H-benzo[b]carbazole-3-carbonitrile
(7). 1-Methyl-4-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-pyrazole
(34 mg, 0.16 mmol) and 37 (60 mg, 0.13 mmol) were dissolved in
1,4-dioxane (5 mL) and 2 M Na2CO3 satd aq solution (0.17 mL, 0.34 mmol)
and thoroughly degassed. Pd(dppf)Cl2 (6 mg, 0.008 mmol) and t-Bu-XPhos (4
mg, 0.005 mmol) were added, and the mixture was heated to 100 °C in a
sealed vial. After the mixture was stirred for 1 h, LC/MS analysis
indicated the reaction was finished. The reaction mixture was filtered
through Celite and purified by reversed-phase HPLC using a gradient of
30-100% CH3CN/H2O with 0.035% TFA.
9-Ethyl-6,6-dimethyl-11-oxo-8-(1-(tetrahydro-2H-pyran-4-yl)-1H-pyrazol-4-yl)-6,11-dihydro-5H-benzo[b]carbazole-3-carbonitrile
(29). The procedure used to prepare compound 7 was used to prepare
compound 29. Purification by reversed-phase HPLC using a gradient of
10-80% CH3CN/H2O with 0.035% TFA gave the desired compound as a beige
solid (48 mg, 76% yield). 1H NMR (DMSO-d 6, 400 MHz) δ 12.76 (s, 1H),
8.34 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 8.18 (s, 1H), 8.11 (s, 1H), 8.01 (s, 1H), 7.78
(d, J = 8 Hz, 2H), 7.62 (d, J = 8 Hz, 1H), 4.49 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 1H), 3.98
(m, 4H), 3.50 (m, 4H), 2.85 (q, J = 7.2 Hz, 2H), 1.76 (s, 6H), 1.23 (t, J
= 8 Hz, 3H); MS m/z 465.84 [M + 1].
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM sealed tube used
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Discovery of Inhibitors That Overcome the G1202R Anaplastic Lymphoma
Kinase Resistance Mutation
